From IBFD:

*Netherlands*

*Netherlands Enacts Amendments to Minimum Tax, Bill to Implement DAC9*The Netherlands has enacted amendments to the Minimum Tax Act and a Bill to Implement DAC9.

The main amendments regarding the Minimum Tax Act include:
–    definitions of “flow-through entities” and “hybrid entities” for Pillar Two purposes;
–    a provision that deferred tax assets arising before the transition year, whether due to a government arrangement or the introduction of a corporate income tax, are excluded from the effective tax rate (ETR) calculation in subsequent years;
–    a provision that under the transitional CbCR safe harbour, following IF guidance, under certain circumstances, a correction must be made for payments arising from hybrid intra-group transactions (i.e. an anti-avoidance provision);
–    a provision that a group entity will also include a joint venture and the parties associated with the joint venture. Consequently, these group entities are subject to the qualified domestic minimum top-up tax if they are established in the Netherlands and the ETR is below 15%.Measures without retroactive effect include:
–    a rule to determine the GloBE income or loss and the covered tax of a constituent entity;
–    an amendment to the rules determining the scope of net tax expense for the purpose of determining the GloBE income or loss of a constituent entity;
–    a rule for determining the book value in the case of an impairment of assets or liabilities;
–    a measure that regulates when a different book value must be used for the calculation of adjusted movements in deferred tax assets and liabilities compared to the book value used in financial reporting;
–    a rule on deferred tax assets that have arisen before the transition year to the minimum tax because of a government arrangement or the introduction of a company tax;
–    a measure that provides that the utilization of the deferred tax assets must not be included in the determination of the simplified covered taxes for the application of the transitional CbCR safe harbour;
–    a rule connected to the transitional CbCR safe harbour. Under this rule, payments arising from intra-group transactions will, under certain circumstances, be treated as interest for both the payer and the recipient based on their financial reporting; and
–    amendments to the provisions relating to the turnover threshold in the event of a merger of two or more groups.

*DAC9*
The government published a separate bill to implement [Amending Directive to the 2011 Directive on Administrative Cooperation (2025/872) (DAC9)|https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=OJ:L_202500872].DAC9 provides for a framework for streamlining filing obligations and facilitating the exchange of information filed by MNEs and large domestic groups under the [Minimum Taxation Directive (2022/2523)|https://research.ibfd.org/#/doc?url=/linkresolver/static/eulaw_2022_2523_eng__td1].

For previous coverage, _see_ [2026 Tax Plan In Depth: Government Proposes Amendments to Minimum Tax and Bill to Implement DAC9 (17 September 2025)|https://research.ibfd.org/#/doc?url=/linkresolver/static/tns_2025-09-17_nl_6], [Lower House of Parliament Adopts Amendments to Minimum Tax Act and Bill to Implement DAC9 (27 November 2025)|https://research.ibfd.org/#/doc?url=/linkresolver/static/tns_2025-11-27_nl_1] and [Upper House of Parliament Adopts Amendments to Minimum Tax, Bill Implementing DAC9 (17 December 2025)|https://research.ibfd.org/#/doc?url=/linkresolver/static/tns_2025-12-17_nl_1].

The lower house of the parliament adopted the plan on 27 November (_see_ [Lower House of Parliament Adopts Amendments to Minimum Tax Act and Bill to Implement DAC9 (27 November 2025)|https://research.ibfd.org/#/doc?url=/linkresolver/static/tns_2025-11-27_nl_1]); the upper house adopted it on 16 December 2025 (_see_ [Upper House of Parliament Adopts Amendments to Minimum Tax, Bill Implementing DAC9 (17 December 2025)|https://research.ibfd.org/#/doc?url=/linkresolver/static/tns_2025-12-17_nl_1]).

The full text of the enacted laws, which were published in Official Gazette nos. 448 and 449 of 23 December 2025, are available [here|https://zoek.officielebekendmakingen.nl/stb-2025-448.html] (changes to minimum tax) and [here|https://zoek.officielebekendmakingen.nl/stb-2025-449.html] (DAC9).

_Note_: The Tax Plan is the official name of the set of tax measures the government proposes annually. It consists of a set of bills (one of which is named “the Tax Plan”) that together are referred to as the Tax Plan package (_pakket Belastingplan_).“”

