The problem lies in how the DSL editor integrates with the rest of the UI and how the save button works.

Every action field and every document rule are independent subtrees that are managed by an {{OperandTreeComponent}} or a {{RuleTreeComponent}}. The changes made the individual operands and rules are propagated up to the entire config trees via callbacks. Here’s a typical flow (taken from {{ActionFieldOperandValue}}:

{noformat}    useEffect(() => {
        try {
            const config = unflattenTree(tree) as OperandConfig;
            onChange(field, config);
        } catch {
            // do not care
        }
    }, [tree, field, onChange]);{noformat}

So if the change made to a tree is not serialiazable – we just ignore it. This means not showing Save button on partial changes. However, if after making a partial change the user adds a proper change to an unrelated field then the {{onChange}} callback is going to be triggered and the save button is going to be show.

We need some sort of a global error tracking mechanism.

